From 53f99ccde76a314cfec99062fc478078fe7a833b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ultimatejeeves <ultimatejeeves@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:19:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/43] JIT: precompile cached code in VM idle time

A cache hit still cost V8 a WebAssembly.Module + Instance (~100 us), the hitch left when a session
first reaches code. The VM thread now instantiates loaded cache entries ahead of use, in first-seen
order, in time the frame limiter would otherwise sleep and while paused (20 ms slices). Each gets
its own link slot pair from an arena; the block that later hits the entry adopts the instance and
points its link slots there (m_wasmLinkSlots is now a pointer). jitCacheSetPrecompile(n) sets how
many (0 = off); stats report precompiled / adopted counts and time.

THPS4 from a save state with a 14k entry cache, VM paused 1.5 s before boot: all 14,176 entries
precompiled in 1.2 s, 14,128 adopted; hitches over 50 ms 13 -> 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
